ummer so  so a different context um and it's i  mean what it probably got the iranians  very cross um but it got gabriella home  so it had a consequence a couple of  months later we'll see what happens on  this one this one um you know we've got  a couple of demands one of them is that  the prime minister acknowledges that  nazis are hostage uh that he starts  punishing the perpetrators that he keeps  his promise to settle the debt um and  that actually you know we're being used  a bargaining chip in the nuclear deal  negotiations that those negotiations  include an explicit promise or  commitment to end hostage taking um  we'll see how the government responds  and and we'll see in the days to come  how is nazalene doing she isn't in jail  issue she's out but she isn't free  that's right she she's at her parents  still um she's had the call to say you  know you're convicted but she hasn't yet  had the call to say come to prison um  and and hopefully that won't come just  yet  um how she doing she probably gone  through a range of motions shock  then anger  and then kind of a sadness that this has  come to this and how long and where we  are still  um and obviously now i'm in a bit of  worry as a wife as to what's going on  and where things will go it you know  hunger strikes certainly it's an extreme  act um and it's always a bit precarious  at the beginning so uh yeah it's a  stressful thing for us all  it must have been quite a difficult  decision to come to  yeah um you know it it's  um i mean we did one what two years ago  two and a half years ago i have to say i  thought that would be a unique  experience and that  you know when the prime minister came  into office he would uh resolve our case  and keep his word um  here we are two years on it  it's been something that  we have been racking our brains as to  what else we could do and probably the  trigger was last weekend  okay richard thank you so much for  talking to us
 

